inema 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" aria-current=\"page\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"upload-fbx-and-obj\">Upload FBX and OBJ<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#upload-fbx-and-obj\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Upload the FBX or OBJ your tool already exports — 3ds Max, Maya, Revit,\nSketchUp, Cinema 4D, Unity, Unreal, Blender — and get a share link. We\nconvert it to glTF on our side, then it takes the same road as a GLB:\nright-sized, classified, and shown in <a href=\"/docs/guides/fidelity-mode\" id=\"lnk-fidelity-mode\">Fidelity mode</a>\n(a product) or streamed (a room, a building, a street).</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-upload\">What to upload<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-to-upload\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>You have</th><th>Upload</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>an FBX with its textures <strong>embedded</strong> (Max/Maya &quot;Embed Media&quot;, Blender &quot;Embed Textures&quot;)</td><td>the <code>.fbx</code></td></tr><tr><td>an FBX whose textures are separate files</td><td>a <strong><code>.zip</code></strong> with the <code>.fbx</code> and its texture folder, as the exporter left them</td></tr><tr><td>an OBJ</td><td>a <strong><code>.zip</code></strong> with the <code>.obj</code>, its <code>.mtl</code> and the textures. An <code>.obj</code> alone converts, with plain colours</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul><li><strong>FBX</strong>: binary or ASCII, FBX 2011–2020 (file versions 7.1–7.7).\nFBX 2010 and older (6.x) is refused with a message — re-export as FBX\n2014 or newer.</li><li><strong>Zip</strong>: standard Deflate or stored entries, no password. Other scene\nfiles riding along in the zip (<code>.max</code>, <code>.blend</code>, a USD or glTF copy) are\nignored; if both an <code>.fbx</code> and an <code>.obj</code> are inside, the FBX is used\n(send <code>X-Verse-Kind: obj</code> to pick the OBJ).</li><li><strong>Texture paths</strong> in an FBX or MTL often point at the author&#39;s disk\n(<code>C:\\Users\\…\\Textures\\Brick.PNG</code>). They are resolved against the files\nin the zip by name, case-insensitively, wherever they sit in it.</li></ul>\n<p>The same door as every format: drop the file on the upload screen (the\n<strong>FBX</strong> and <strong>OBJ</strong> chips say <em>converted on our side</em>), <code>POST /v1/ingest</code>\n(the bytes are recognised; <code>X-Verse-Kind: fbx</code> | <code>obj</code> is optional), or\n<code>@ctruhtech/verse-sdk</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">const { job } = await verse.upload(zipFile, { kind: &quot;obj&quot;, name: &quot;bistro&quot;, units: &quot;cm&quot; });\nconst rec = await verse.waitForJob(job);\n// rec.url     → the share link\n// rec.convert → { kind: &quot;obj&quot;, schema, products, triangles, materials, images,\n//                 missingTextures, units, size, seconds, … }\n// rec.fixes   → &quot;Converted the OBJ on our side (from the zip): 1,306 objects, …&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<p>The build shows a <strong>converting</strong> stage (<em>unpacking the zip</em> → <em>reading\nthe model</em> → <em>writing the glTF</em>), then the usual ladder. Limits are the\nordinary ones: 512 MB per upload (a zip counts at its compressed size),\n15 minutes for the conversion (<code>VERSE_CONVERT_TIMEOUT_S</code>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-comes-across-and-what-fbx-obj-can-t-carry\">What comes across — and what FBX / OBJ can&#39;t carry<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-comes-across-and-what-fbx-obj-can-t-carry\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>FBX</th><th>OBJ + MTL</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Geometry, normals, UVs, object names and hierarchy</td><td>yes</td><td>yes (<code>o</code> objects and <code>g</code> groups become objects)</td></tr><tr><td>Units</td><td><strong>from the file</strong> (<code>UnitScaleFactor</code>): centimetre files from Max / Maya land in metres</td><td><strong>none in the format</strong>: a model wider than 1,000 units is read as centimetres (wider than 100,000 as millimetres) and the fix line says so; <code>X-Verse-Units: m | cm | mm | in | ft</code> (SDK <code>units</code>) overrides</td></tr><tr><td>Up axis</td><td><strong>from the file</strong> (<code>UpAxis</code>): Z-up files stand upright</td><td>Y-up, as the format expects</td></tr><tr><td>Base colour, metallic, roughness, emissive</td><td>Phong / Lambert values; <strong>3ds Max Physical</strong>, <strong>Maya Stingray PBS</strong> and <strong>Arnold</strong> base values and maps (colour, normal, metalness, roughness, emission) are read from the file and mapped to PBR</td><td><code>Kd</code>, <code>Ke</code>, the PBR extension lines (<code>Pr</code>, <code>Pm</code>, <code>Ps</code>, <code>Pc</code>) and the <code>map_*</code> textures</td></tr><tr><td>Textures</td><td>embedded ones always; separate files when zipped. TIFF, TGA, BMP, DDS and EXR are re-encoded as PNG</td><td>when zipped</td></tr><tr><td>Transparency</td><td><code>TransparencyFactor</code> / opacity → alpha</td><td><code>d</code> → alpha. <code>Tf</code> (transmission filter) is <strong>not</strong> turned into glass — most exporters write <code>Tf 1 1 1</code> by default</td></tr><tr><td>Animation and skins</td><td>node animation and skinned meshes play (one clip with every moving object in it); static &quot;Take 001&quot; takes are dropped so a still scene is not published as animated</td><td>— (OBJ has none)</td></tr><tr><td>Lights and cameras</td><td>lights come across; cameras are not used</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Not carried</strong></td><td>renderer-only shaders (V-Ray, Corona, Redshift, Arnold node graphs beyond their base values), procedural maps, displacement, layered materials, photometric (IES) lights, more than one animation take, morph targets (shape keys are kept in the file but the streamed viewer does not play them)</td><td>anything beyond the MTL</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Emission strength and the clearcoat of a 3ds Max Physical / Stingray /\nArnold material become the matching <code>KHR_materials_*</code> extensions and\nrender as listed in <a href=\"/docs/guides/what-you-can-upload#what-is-rendered\" id=\"lnk-what-is-rendered\">what is rendered</a>.\nPhong specular is not PBR data: it is set to the neutral value rather\nthan turned into <code>KHR_materials_specular</code>.</p>\n<p>Missing textures never fail an upload: the link builds, those surfaces\nkeep their colour, and the record names them (<code>convert.missingTextures</code>,\nand the fix line: <em>&quot;3 textures the model names were not in the upload\n(Brick_Diff.png, …) — upload a .zip with the texture folder to include\nthem&quot;</em>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-the-conversion-works-and-why-blender\">How the conversion works (and why Blender)<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-the-conversion-works-and-why-blender\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<p><code>tools/model-convert/convert.mjs</code> unpacks a zip (zip-slip and zip-bomb\nguarded), transcodes an <strong>ASCII</strong> FBX to binary, repairs MTL texture\npaths, and runs <strong>headless Blender 5.0</strong> (<code>blender -b</code>) to import the\nmodel and export glTF. Blender reads binary FBX only, so the ASCII→binary\nstep is our own (<code>fbx-ascii.mjs</code>): ASCII and binary FBX are the same node\ntree, so the transcode is lossless — it keeps the 3ds Max Physical and\nStingray properties that an importer round trip would drop.</p>\n<p>We measured three converters on the same files before choosing (the gate\nfixture: a textured cube, a metallic sphere, an emissive lamp and a\nskinned, animated bar, exported metres Y-up and centimetres Z-up; the\nUnity <em>Boat Attack</em> FBX files from 3ds Max; and the Intel Sponza release,\na 929 MB ASCII FBX with 3ds Max Physical materials, 3.75 M triangles and\n144 textures):</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><strong>Blender 5.0 (chosen)</strong></th><th>FBX2glTF 0.13 (FBX SDK 2020)</th><th>assimp 6.0</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Units and up axis (cm Z-up fixture → 5 × 2.15 × 2 m)</td><td>correct</td><td>correct</td><td><strong>100× too big</strong> (500 × 215 × 200: no FBX unit conversion)</td></tr><tr><td>Materials on the fixture</td><td>gold metallic 1 / roughness 0.3, lamp emission ×4 — exact</td><td><strong>metallic 0.4 on every material</strong>, roughness from shininess (0.2), duplicated materials</td><td>texture darkened (base factor 0.8), metallic lost, extra specular/volume extensions</td></tr><tr><td>Materials on Unity / Max files</td><td>sane Phong mapping</td><td>the Unity cliffs <strong>glow white</strong> (emissive 1)</td><td>roughness <strong>−0.6</strong> (invalid)</td></tr><tr><td>ASCII FBX</td><td>via our lossless transcoder</td><td>read, but the external texture was lost</td><td>read</td></tr><tr><td>OBJ</td><td>correct (cm OBJ read as cm by rule)</td><td><strong>100× too small</strong> (0.05 m)</td><td>correct, but a phantom default material</td></tr><tr><td>Animation / skins</td><td>kept (one clip)</td><td>kept (1-channel stubs per take)</td><td>kept</td></tr><tr><td>Sponza 929 MB ASCII FBX</td><td><strong>72 s, 3.5 GB peak</strong> (zip in, all 28 Physical materials mapped, 95 maps incl. normal / roughness / metalness, 36.2 × 19.9 × 23.8 m)</td><td>182 s (x86 build under Rosetta), 2.9 GB, 49 maps, base colour halved</td><td>26 s but <strong>7.2 GB</strong>, 3,625 m wide, roughness −2.2</td></tr><tr><td>Fixture conversion</td><td>0.5–1 s, 220 MB</td><td>0.05–0.12 s, 14 MB</td><td>0.01–0.03 s, 7 MB</td></tr><tr><td>In the image</td><td>+360 MB compressed (pruned Linux build)</td><td>+6 MB, but bundles the proprietary Autodesk FBX SDK; x86-only</td><td>+10 MB</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Blender is the slowest and largest, and the only one that got units,\naxes and materials right on every file — the criteria that decide whether\nthe link looks like the model. The image cost is in the &quot;In the image&quot;\nrow above.</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-it-does-not-work\">When it does not work<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#when-it-does-not-work\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Why</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><em>This FBX or OBJ file isn&#39;t one we can read</em> (<code>model_invalid</code>)</td><td>not FBX/OBJ bytes, FBX older than 2011, a zip with no <code>.fbx</code>/<code>.obj</code>, an unreadable file</td><td>re-export (FBX 2014+ binary is the safest), or zip the model itself</td></tr><tr><td><em>We couldn&#39;t convert this file</em> (<code>convert_failed</code>)</td><td>the converter crashed or ran past 15 minutes</td><td>try again; if it repeats, export GLB from your tool</td></tr><tr><td>the model is 100× too big or too small</td><td>an OBJ in a unit the rule guessed wrong</td><td>upload again with <code>X-Verse-Units</code> (SDK <code>units</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>surfaces are flat colours</td><td>the textures were separate files and not zipped, or the MTL was missing</td><td>zip the model with its texture folder (and <code>.mtl</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#what-to-upload\" id=\"lnk-what-to-upload\">What to upload</a><a href=\"#what-comes-across-and-what-fbx-obj-can-t-carry\" id=\"lnk-what-comes-across-and-what-fbx-obj-can-t\">What comes across — and what FBX / OBJ can't carry</a><a href=\"#how-the-conversion-works-and-why-blender\" id=\"lnk-how-the-conversion-works-and-why-blender\">How the conversion works (and why Blender)</a><a href=\"#when-it-does-not-work\" id=\"lnk-when-it-does-not-work\">When it does not work</a></aside></section>"}